{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrveVNa1oYd3FQEk2uQn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `metrics/counter.py`, and `tests/test_metrics.py` passes on five consecutive runs. I did not run the test against the original code to confirm it fails there, so the reproduction is unverified.\n\n**Root cause:** `incr()` read the current value, yielded with `time.sleep(0)`, then wrote back `current + by`. Concurrent increments of the same name overwrote each other, so updates were lost. `snapshot()` also copied the dict with no coordination against inserts and removals.\n\n**Change:**\n- **Per-name locks:** each counter name gets its own `threading.Lock`, so `incr()` on one name never waits on another. A small `_registry_lock` guards the lock table and key insertion/removal.\n- **`incr()`** does its read-modify-write under that name's lock.\n- **`get()`** is lock-free. A single dict read is atomic and writers only store whole values.\n- **`snapshot()`** copies `_values` under `_registry_lock` and returns a plain dict, same as before.\n- **`reset()`** takes the name's lock for a single name. With no name, it lists the current keys under the registry lock and resets each one.\n- **API:** `Counter`, `incr`, `get`, `snapshot` and `reset` keep their signatures.\n\n**Choices to review:**\n- I removed the `time.sleep(0)` that simulated work inside the read-modify-write. It only widened the race window and has no place in a locked section.\n- `snapshot()` is consistent per counter, not across counters. Each value is whole, but two counters may be read at slightly different moments. A cross-counter consistent snapshot would need a global lock, which you asked me to avoid.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13059,"cache_read_input_tokens":27864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13059},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84d93de5-258c-4e3a-b58b-75eb9dbf1a0c","uuid":"08b45781-6804-44d8-86f2-eb2b077d84d5","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:48:06.301Z","request_id":"req_011CfrveV7CeLVBxgmFjAUGM"}
